## Key Learnings
1. Pekko's CircuitBreaker Closed state resets its failure count to zero on every success, so it trips on consecutive failures, which the reconciliation text for PAT-09 omits.
2. RetrySupport.calculateDelay applies the jitter factor after capping at maxBackoff, so with a nonzero random factor the delay can exceed maxBackoff, and no actor-tests spec tests jitter.
3. Pekko's ByteArraySerializer returns the same array uncopied and SerializeSpec asserts same-instance identity, which contradicts the copy semantics in the SER-09 acceptance criteria.
4. The nested-deserialization depth limit has an oracle spec only in the remote module, so claiming that no applicable oracle exists conflicts with the literal wording of ADR 0033 D13.
5. Neither LookupClassification nor ScanningClassification depends on EventStream or on each other in Pekko, and EventBusSpec observes duplicates and unsubscribe results but never publish ordering.
